  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Indonesia&apos;s Health Care Referral Network (SIHREN)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall HSS Program objective is to increase the availability of functional equipment in public health facilities and to improve the utilization of public health services across Indonesia.

The Program Objective was developed based on the results chain responding to the problem statement, capturing the challenges experienced across Indonesia&#x2019;s public health system, which require to be urgently addressed through this Project: &#x2018;Public health and laboratory facilities, across all levels of the public healthcare system and across the country, currently face significant gaps in the availability of critical equipment, without the necessary operational skills and maintenance capacity for this equipment, which is also a key driver of the severe underutilization of these facilities.&#x2019; The primary beneficiaries of this project are the entire population of Indonesia, and secondary beneficiaries are health workers at all levels of the health system.
The SIHREN Project aims to enhance the physical and service capacity of the health referral system in Indonesia. This objective ensures equal access to quality healthcare services in all districts, cities, and provinces, including addressing health emergencies and pandemics. Secondly, the Project seeks to decrease the incidence of cancer, heart disease, stroke, and uronephrol</narrative>
  </description>
